x.c('requirements_first_slice',1,24,42,'Generic requirements first slice','Includes event payloads,RequirementLedger,stable identities/typed relations,staged authority,existing-topology spans,edge environments,obligation/materialization/execution/evidence,binding,fold/residual over assurance/continuation,completeness,queries,compatibility wrappers. Excludes odd_glc,downstream migration,KAOS/ReqIF/GSN/GRL exchange,editors and Product semantic judgment.')
x.c('requirement_term_and_context',2,46,64,'Requirement term and staged context','Requirement events are sole writes; ledger replays them. Terms retain stable id,source/digest,relations,spans,context,evidence policy,projection. Relations are typed; unknown kinds reject before projection. Authority fragments retain origin,scope,digest,promotion,applies-to,routing without automatically becoming closeable terms. Destination topology is HOW constraint framework, not WHAT or tenant-only convention.')
x.q('span_and_edge_projection',2,58,70,'requirement_term_and_context','Spans bind existing function/vector and retain lineage across function/vector/frame/zoom/foldback/alias, never new public target/topology. Edge environments derive staged context,active spans,prior folds,residuals,compatible obligations. Active edge projection deterministic on ledger/admitted edge. Obligation/materialization/schedule/evidence expectations are read models. Stronger active role policy supersedes matching weaker design target at same projection/path; admitted schedule commands take precedence over fallback for same projection.')
x.c('requirement_evidence_binding',2,72,80,'Generic proof evidence binding','Distinguish subject-artifact,verifier-artifact,verifier-execution,semantic interpretation. Compatibility names asset/test_source/test_execution denote generic roles, not software policy. Path/tool/pass cannot substitute roles. Current admitted evidence supersedes empty/stale predecessor without erasing history; byproducts nonclosing unless explicitly admitted. A verifier-root file is verifier evidence only under active admitted proof relation for root/role; artifact may be partial nonclosing before execution discoverability.')
x.c('fold_residual_attenuation',2,82,90,'Requirement fold, residual and attenuation','Folds map existing assurance/continuation/evaluate-next, no second decisions. Residual preserves remaining span,pressure,owner,evidence,source fold, no retry/continuation/reentry controller. Movement classes: unchanged,narrowed,transformed,moved-to-prerequisite,escalated,cleared. Assurance-case read model projects claim/context/evidence/fold/residual, no writes.')
x.q('deterministic_requirement_limits',2,90,104,'requirements_algebra','F_D total admitted-state outcomes include valid,malformed,unknown-state-rejected,incomplete,stale/superseded,contradictory,semantic-assessment-required,semantic-residual-preserved,human-decision-required,nonclosing. Unknown/unclassified rejects,classifies or routes typed F_P/F_H before evaluation. Fail closed missing span,evidence-policy,context routing,destination,proof relation,fold-attenuation coverage. Obstacle/conflict gates check only admitted structural resolution; F_P owns ambiguous plausibility/admission. Compatibility obligation/residual wrappers cannot own closure/retry/continuation/reentry. Queries expose requirements/obligations/targets/schedules/evidence/folds/residual/attenuation/claims without archive parsing. Product meaning comes through authored terms/context/functions/evidence/F_P/F_H/plugins, never unknown-syntax inference. First slice needs worked trace declaration→edge→obligation→evidence→fold→residual/attenuation→query.')
x.c('requirements_public_route',2,106,122,'Pure public requirements route','Downstream declares GTL inputs and queries admitted truth; admission/projection commands emitting requirement/fold/residual/disposition stay runtime-internal. Facades reconcile one-to-one with existing symbols or ratified gaps, not another function/carrier catalog,ledger or closure surface.')
x.q('nominal_refs_and_real_path_admission',2,110,122,'requirements_public_route requirement_evidence_binding','Requirement/evidence/fold/residual/disposition/scope refs are nominal unforgeable inputs; command boundaries resolve replay truth and recompute digest. Unknown/dangling/stale/superseded/mismatched reject; supplied ref/sourceEventRef/digest alone is not admission. Bind evidence with admitted runtime event and requirement projection refs; reject booleans,path shape,pass/fail closure,arbitrary truth strings. Fold consumes admitted binding and assurance decision refs, never manual/downstream/query closure. Runtime real traversal including applicable edge-close emits fold/residual/disposition; query cannot invent lazily. Lifecycle disposition is read-only over admitted residual/fold/continuation/reentry, not writer/enum/controller. Policy affecting it must be admitted runtime-policy/F_H refs; free strings inert labels only.')
x.q('semantic_authority_and_case_distinctions',2,124,132,'requirements_algebra requirements_public_route','F_D may validate/admit/reject/project/replay/join/guard, not author/infer meaning,missing requirements,satisfaction,residual acceptability,semantic action or command-success closure. F_P/F_H arrive as admitted provenance/digest refs, never deterministic reconstruction of their authority. Empty assurance fold is no_evidence, distinct from blocked,partial,satisfied,deferred,repriced,no-close-preserved. Joined lifecycle query returns environment/obligation/targets/schedules/evidence/folds/claims/residual/attenuation/disposition/sources without events. Negative proof covers downstream emission,forged refs,digest mismatch,boolean admission,manual assurance,query-lazy truth,F_D semantic inference.')
x.q('requirement_graph_parent_and_span_read_models',2,134,142,'requirements_algebra requirements_public_route','Graph reuses admitted RequirementTerm/Relation, never second KAOS/goal/decomposition/obstacle/graph kernel or writable refinement. Edge environments project active parent-child relation pressure with terms/spans as query input, not selection/continuation/reentry. Parent fold/residual is read-only aggregation of admitted children/leaves; counting or command success cannot mint parent writer. Multi-requirement reads expose graph,relations,leaf/parent state,residual/sources without internal commands. Span-lineage reuses TraversalSpan and exposes id,function,vectors/indexes,nodes,frames,zoom,foldback,aliases,active status; no identity inference from index,string matching,prompt,Product maps/names.')
